<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Notation</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the rest of this appendix, we use the following notation:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We denote by <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> the standard centered and unit variance Gaussian measure on <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Explicitly, for any <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\gamma(\mathbf{x})=(2\pi)^{-d/2}\exp\!\left(-\tfrac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(\mathbf{x})=(2\pi)^{-d/2}\exp\!\left(-\tfrac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The space <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma):=\left\{f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}\;\middle|\;\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|f(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}_{2}\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})&lt;\infty\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma):=\left\{f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}\;\middle|\;\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|f(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}_{2}\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})&lt;\infty\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where functions are identified up to equality <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-almost everywhere.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We equip <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> with an inner product defined as,</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f,g\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}:=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(\mathbf{x})\,g(\mathbf{x})\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f,g\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}:=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(\mathbf{x})\,g(\mathbf{x})\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">making it a Hilbert space <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(L^{2}(\gamma),\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(L^{2}(\gamma),\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> inner product induces the following <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>-norm,</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|_{L^{2}(\gamma)}=\left(\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|f(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}_{2}\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})\right)^{1/2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|_{L^{2}(\gamma)}=\left(\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|f(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}_{2}\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})\right)^{1/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any sequence of distributions <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{R}_{+}}\in(\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d}))^{\mathbb{R}_{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{R}_{+}}\in(\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d}))^{\mathbb{R}_{+}}</annotation></semantics></math> and any fixed <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\star}\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\star}\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{t})_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{t})_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and denote <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}\underset{t\to\infty}{\overset{\mathcal{W}_{2}}{\longrightarrow}}\mu^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒲</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}\underset{t\to\infty}{\overset{\mathcal{W}_{2}}{\longrightarrow}}\mu^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> if,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu_{t},\mu^{\star})\underset{t\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu_{t},\mu^{\star})\underset{t\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Extended Background and Preliminary Results</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix, we provide a detailed background of the mathematical tools and the classical results underlying our proofs.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that, for each generation <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the forward process <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{X}_{t}^{i})_{t\in[0,T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{X}_{t}^{i})_{t\in[0,T]}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as a solution of the following variance-preserving Ornstein-Uhlenbeck diffusion initialized at the mixture distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\mathbf{X}_{t}^{i}=-\tfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{X}_{t}^{i}\,\mathrm{d}t+\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t},\qquad\mathbf{X}_{0}^{i}\sim q_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\mathbf{X}_{t}^{i}=-\tfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{X}_{t}^{i}\,\mathrm{d}t+\mathrm{d}\mathbf{B}_{t},\qquad\mathbf{X}_{0}^{i}\sim q_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then, integrating (<a href="#A2.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{i}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}^{i}_{0}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z},\qquad\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{i}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}^{i}_{0}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z},\qquad\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The corresponding transition kernel can thus be written as,</p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\mathcal{N}\!\left(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{x},(1-e^{-t})\mathbf{I}_{d}\right)(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.798em;" width="0.798em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\mathcal{N}\!\left(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{x},(1-e^{-t})\mathbf{I}_{d}\right)(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Markov semigroup.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The transition kernel <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> defines a Markov semigroup <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> acting on test functions <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t}\varphi)(\mathbf{x}):=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{y})\,\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\mathbb{E}\big[\varphi(\mathbf{X}_{t}^{i})\mid\mathbf{X}_{0}^{i}=\mathbf{x}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t}\varphi)(\mathbf{x}):=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{y})\,\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\mathbb{E}\big[\varphi(\mathbf{X}_{t}^{i})\mid\mathbf{X}_{0}^{i}=\mathbf{x}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The family <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the semigroup property <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t+s}=P_{t}P_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t+s}=P_{t}P_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}=\mathrm{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Id</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}=\mathrm{Id}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sampling operator on probability measures.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The adjoint of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> acts on test functions. On the other hand, the OU diffusion (<a href="#A2.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) defines sampling operators <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t\in[t_{0},T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t\in[t_{0},T]}</annotation></semantics></math>, acting on probability measures <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and defined by,</p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu(A):=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},A)\,\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}),\qquad A\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu(A):=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},A)\,\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}),\qquad A\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Equivalently,</p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu=\mathrm{Law}\!\big(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}_{0}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z}\big),\qquad\mathbf{X}_{0}\sim\mu,\;\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d}),\;\mathbf{X}_{0}\perp\!\!\!\perp\mathbf{Z}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.782em;" width="1.782em"><mi>Law</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu=\mathrm{Law}\!\big(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}_{0}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z}\big),\qquad\mathbf{X}_{0}\sim\mu,\;\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d}),\;\mathbf{X}_{0}\perp\!\!\!\perp\mathbf{Z}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The operator <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sampling operator used throughout the paper. Given its central role in this work, we collect its properties in the following proposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Basic properties of the OU sampling operator)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Ornstein–Uhlenbeck sampling operator <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in (<a href="#A2.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>),
satisfies the following properties.</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Linearity.</span><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For any two probability measures </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\nu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and scalars </span><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}(a\mu+b\nu)=a\,\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu+b\,\mathcal{U}_{t}\nu." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}(a\mu+b\nu)=a\,\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu+b\,\mathcal{U}_{t}\nu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Semigroup property.</span><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For all </span><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t+s}=\mathcal{U}_{t}\mathcal{U}_{s},\qquad\mathcal{U}_{0}=\mathbf{I}_{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t+s}=\mathcal{U}_{t}\mathcal{U}_{s},\qquad\mathcal{U}_{0}=\mathbf{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Weak duality identity.</span><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For any bounded measurable test function </span><math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and every finite measure </span><math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{y})\,(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}(P_{t}\varphi)(\mathbf{x})\,\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{y})\,(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}(P_{t}\varphi)(\mathbf{x})\,\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iv)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Second moments preservation.</span><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
If </span><math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=e^{-t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}\,\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})+d(1-e^{-t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=e^{-t}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}\,\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})+d(1-e^{-t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(v)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Gaussian invariant measure.</span><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let </span><math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then </span><math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\gamma=\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\gamma=\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(vi)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Action in <math id="A2.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span><span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For any </span><math id="A2.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, writing </span><math id="A2.I1.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\mathrm{d}\mu/\mathrm{d}\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\mathrm{d}\mu/\mathrm{d}\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}=P_{t}f." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}=P_{t}f.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(vii)</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Continuity in time.</span><span id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For a fixed </span><math id="A2.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and a fixed </span><math id="A2.I1.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in[0,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in[0,t]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, one has that,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu\underset{t\to s}{\overset{\mathcal{W}_{2}}{\longrightarrow}}\mathcal{U}_{s}\mu." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">s</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒲</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu\underset{t\to s}{\overset{\mathcal{W}_{2}}{\longrightarrow}}\mathcal{U}_{s}\mu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I1.i7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu\underset{t\to 0}{\overset{\mathcal{W}_{2}}{\longrightarrow}}\mu." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒲</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu\underset{t\to 0}{\overset{\mathcal{W}_{2}}{\longrightarrow}}\mu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(i) Linearity.</em><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> be two probability distributions on <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> two scalars. Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be any measurable set in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then using (<a href="#A2.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}(a\mu+b\nu)(A)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},A)\,(a\mu+b\nu)(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}(a\mu+b\nu)(A)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},A)\,(a\mu+b\nu)(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Looking at (<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>), <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is linear in its first argument, yielding,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}(a\mu+b\nu)(A)=a\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},A)\,\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})+b\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},A)\,\nu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})=a\,\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu+b\,\mathcal{U}_{t}\nu." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}(a\mu+b\nu)(A)=a\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},A)\,\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})+b\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},A)\,\nu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})=a\,\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu+b\,\mathcal{U}_{t}\nu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(ii) Semigroup property.</em><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and consider <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, fix two independently distributed Gaussian random variables <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},Z_{2}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},Z_{2}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and fix <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,t\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,t\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying successively <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{U}_{t}\mathcal{U}_{s}\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{U}_{t}\mathcal{U}_{s}\mu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{-t/2}\left(e^{-s/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-s}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{1}\right)+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{-t/2}\left(e^{-s/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-s}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{1}\right)+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{-(t+s)/2}\mathbf{X}+\left(e^{-t/2}\sqrt{1-e^{-s}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{1}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{2}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{-(t+s)/2}\mathbf{X}+\left(e^{-t/2}\sqrt{1-e^{-s}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{1}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent standard Gaussians, the variable <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left(e^{-t/2}\sqrt{1-e^{-s}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{1}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(e^{-t/2}\sqrt{1-e^{-s}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{1}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z}_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is a centered Gaussian with covariance</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-t}(1-e^{-s})\mathbf{I}_{d}+(1-e^{-t})\mathbf{I}_{d}=(1-e^{-(t+s)})\mathbf{I}_{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-t}(1-e^{-s})\mathbf{I}_{d}+(1-e^{-t})\mathbf{I}_{d}=(1-e^{-(t+s)})\mathbf{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Denoting <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, the resulting law is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\mathcal{U}_{s}\mu=\mathrm{Law}\!\left(e^{-(t+s)/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-(t+s)}}\,\mathbf{Z}\right)=\mathcal{U}_{t+s}\mu." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.782em;" width="1.782em"><mi>Law</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\mathcal{U}_{s}\mu=\mathrm{Law}\!\left(e^{-(t+s)/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-(t+s)}}\,\mathbf{Z}\right)=\mathcal{U}_{t+s}\mu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">This being true for any <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, one has that <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\mathcal{U}_{s}=\mathcal{U}_{t+s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\mathcal{U}_{s}=\mathcal{U}_{t+s}</annotation></semantics></math>. The identity <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{0}=\mathbf{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{0}=\mathbf{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> follows directly from
the definition.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(iii) Weak duality identity.</em><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text">
By the definitions of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Markov semigroup. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{y})\,(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\underbrace{\left(\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{y})\,\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})\right)}_{:=P_{t}\varphi(\mathbf{x})}\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}(P_{t}\varphi)(\mathbf{x})\,\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{y})\,(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\underbrace{\left(\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{y})\,\mathcal{K}_{t}(\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})\right)}_{:=P_{t}\varphi(\mathbf{x})}\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}(P_{t}\varphi)(\mathbf{x})\,\mu(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}=P_{t}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}=P_{t}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> in the usual measure-function duality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(iv) Second moments preservation.</em><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Fix <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim\mu\perp\!\!\!\perp\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mpadded style="width:0.518em;" width="0.518em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim\mu\perp\!\!\!\perp\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. Letting <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{Y}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, by the representation of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>). Using the independence of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\|\mathbf{Y}\|^{2}]=e^{-t}\mathbb{E}[\|\mathbf{X}\|^{2}]+d(1-e^{-t})&lt;\infty,\qquad\text{ since }\mathbb{E}[\|\mathbf{X}\|^{2}]&lt;\infty" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> since </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\|\mathbf{Y}\|^{2}]=e^{-t}\mathbb{E}[\|\mathbf{X}\|^{2}]+d(1-e^{-t})&lt;\infty,\qquad\text{ since }\mathbb{E}[\|\mathbf{X}\|^{2}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(v) Gaussian invariance.</em><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> be independent Gaussians, then <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\gamma=\mathrm{Law}(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Law</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\gamma=\mathrm{Law}(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z})</annotation></semantics></math> is a sum of centered independent Gaussians, with covariance <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-t}\mathbf{I}_{d}+(1-e^{-t})\mathbf{I}_{d}=\mathbf{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-t}\mathbf{I}_{d}+(1-e^{-t})\mathbf{I}_{d}=\mathbf{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\gamma=\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\gamma=\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(vi) Action on densities relative to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\mathrm{d}\mu/\mathrm{d}\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\mathrm{d}\mu/\mathrm{d}\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any bounded measurable test function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, by duality,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi\,d(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}P_{t}\varphi\,d\mu=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}P_{t}\varphi(\mathbf{x})f(\mathbf{x})\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi\,d(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}P_{t}\varphi\,d\mu=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}P_{t}\varphi(\mathbf{x})f(\mathbf{x})\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">The OU semigroup is reversible with respect to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is
self-adjoint in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}P_{t}\varphi(\mathbf{x})f(\mathbf{x})\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{x})P_{t}f(\mathbf{x})\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}P_{t}\varphi(\mathbf{x})f(\mathbf{x})\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{x})P_{t}f(\mathbf{x})\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi\,d(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{x})P_{t}f(\mathbf{x})\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi\,d(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\varphi(\mathbf{x})P_{t}f(\mathbf{x})\,\gamma(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since this holds for all bounded measurable <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)}{d\gamma}=P_{t}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)}{d\gamma}=P_{t}f</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(vii) Continuity in time.</em><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Fix <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim\mu,\,\perp\!\!\!\perp\,\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.059em">,</mo><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.448em">⟂</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim\mu,\,\perp\!\!\!\perp\,\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{Y}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}_{t}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}_{t}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and coupling <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> gives,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\big[\|\mathbf{Y}_{t}-\mathbf{X}\|^{2}_{2}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\big[\|\mathbf{Y}_{t}-\mathbf{X}\|^{2}_{2}\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(e^{-t/2}-1)^{2}\mathbb{E}\big[\|\mathbf{X}\|_{2}^{2}\big]+(1-e^{-t})\mathbb{E}\big[\|\mathbf{Z}\|_{2}^{2}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(e^{-t/2}-1)^{2}\mathbb{E}\big[\|\mathbf{X}\|_{2}^{2}\big]+(1-e^{-t})\mathbb{E}\big[\|\mathbf{Z}\|_{2}^{2}\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(e^{-t/2}-1)^{2}\mathbb{E}\big[\|\mathbf{X}\|_{2}^{2}\big]+d(1-e^{-t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(e^{-t/2}-1)^{2}\mathbb{E}\big[\|\mathbf{X}\|_{2}^{2}\big]+d(1-e^{-t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(e^{-t/2}-1)^{2}\mathbb{E}\big[\|\mathbf{X}\|_{2}^{2}\big]+d(1-e^{-t})\underset{t\to 0}{\longrightarrow}0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow></munder><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(e^{-t/2}-1)^{2}\mathbb{E}\big[\|\mathbf{X}\|_{2}^{2}\big]+d(1-e^{-t})\underset{t\to 0}{\longrightarrow}0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">For the more general case, observe that for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, using the semigroup property (proved in </span><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(ii)</span><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.3.3" class="ltx_text">) and the contraction of the OU semigroup in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition B.5 (Wasserstein contraction of OU semigroup []). ‣ B.3 Wasserstein-2 Geometry ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>), one has that,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mathcal{U}_{s}\mu)=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{U}_{\min(s,t)}\mathcal{U}_{|t-s|}\mu,\mathcal{U}_{\min(s,t)}\mu)\leq\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{U}_{|t-s|}\mu,\mu)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mathcal{U}_{s}\mu)=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{U}_{\min(s,t)}\mathcal{U}_{|t-s|}\mu,\mathcal{U}_{\min(s,t)}\mu)\leq\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{U}_{|t-s|}\mu,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">which tends to zero as <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|t-s|\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|t-s|\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> by the previous argument.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Role of the Gaussian distribution and Decomposition in the Hermite Polynomial Basis</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We refer the reader to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> for a detailed review of the properties that we recall in the following.
In our context, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> plays a special role because, as established in Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, it is the <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">unique invariant measure</span> of the Ornstein–Uhlenbeck process, i.e. the unique distribution such that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}(\gamma)=\gamma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}(\gamma)=\gamma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hermite polynomials.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Hermite polynomials are a family of polynomials that play a key role in the analysis of Gaussian Hilbert spaces, and hence, because of the central role of Gaussians in diffusion processes, in the theory of Markov operators. The multivariate Hermite polynomials <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{H_{\mathbf{n}}\}_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{H_{\mathbf{n}}\}_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{d})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=(x_{1},\ldots,x_{d})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by,</p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{x})=\prod_{j=1}^{d}H_{n_{j}}(x_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{x})=\prod_{j=1}^{d}H_{n_{j}}(x_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the degree-<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> univariate Hermite polynomial defined for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> as,</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{k}(x)=(-1)^{k}e^{x^{2}/2}\frac{\mathrm{d}^{k}}{\mathrm{d}x^{k}}e^{-x^{2}/2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}(x)=(-1)^{k}e^{x^{2}/2}\frac{\mathrm{d}^{k}}{\mathrm{d}x^{k}}e^{-x^{2}/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now state two key properties that make these polynomials important analytic tools, the proofs of which can be find in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>. The first one is that they form an orthogonal basis of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Orthogonal Basis of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\sum_{\mathbf{n}}\langle f,H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\sum_{\mathbf{n}}\langle f,H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the scalar product in the Hilbert space <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The second key property is that Hermite polynomials are eigenfunctions of the OU semigroup <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t})_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t})_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined in (<a href="#A2.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Markov semigroup. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Diagonalization of the OU semigroup)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each multi-index <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote the degree of a multivariate Hermite polynomial <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\mathbf{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathbf{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbf{n}|=n_{1}+\cdots+n_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{n}|=n_{1}+\cdots+n_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}H_{\mathbf{n}}=e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t/2}H_{\mathbf{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}H_{\mathbf{n}}=e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t/2}H_{\mathbf{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In other words, multivariate Hermite polynomials are the eigenfunctions of the semigroup <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t})_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t})_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, associated with the eigenvalue <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t/2}</annotation></semantics></math> for polynomials of degree <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbf{n}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{n}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In the context of this work, we are mainly interested in the effect of Hermite polynomials on the sampling operators <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. By combining Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition B.3 (Diagonalization of the OU semigroup). ‣ Hermite polynomials. ‣ B.2 Role of the Gaussian distribution and Decomposition in the Hermite Polynomial Basis ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, one has that, for any <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\sum_{\mathbf{n}}\langle f,H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad P_{t}f=\sum_{\mathbf{n}}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t/2}\langle f,H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\sum_{\mathbf{n}}\langle f,H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad P_{t}f=\sum_{\mathbf{n}}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t/2}\langle f,H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, combining this result with <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vi)</span> in Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we obtain a spectral representation of the action of the sampling operator <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> on probability measures.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\ll\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\ll\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\tfrac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}\in L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\tfrac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}\in L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, then,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t/2}\langle f,H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t/2}\langle f,H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This provides a complete spectral characterization of the OU dynamics.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Wasserstein-2 Geometry</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The space of probability measures on <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with finite second moment, denoted <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, is equipped with the Wasserstein-2 distance defined for all <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\nu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\nu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> as,</p>
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)=\inf_{\pi\in\Pi(\mu,\nu)}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,\pi(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)=\inf_{\pi\in\Pi(\mu,\nu)}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,\pi(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi(\mu,\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi(\mu,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of couplings of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>.
Altogether, the space <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d}),\mathcal{W}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d}),\mathcal{W}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is a complete separable metric space <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A key property used in this work is the contraction of the OU transition operator <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t\in[0,T]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t\in[0,T]}</annotation></semantics></math> in the above Wasserstein-2 geometry.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Wasserstein contraction of OU semigroup <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Ornstein–Uhlenbeck sampling operator defined in (<a href="#A2.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>). Then for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\nu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\nu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mathcal{U}_{t}\nu\bigr)\leq e^{-t/2}\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu,\nu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>ν</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mathcal{U}_{t}\nu\bigr)\leq e^{-t/2}\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu,\nu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> be an optimal coupling of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu,\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. a joint distribution on <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the marginals satisfy <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}\sim\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}\sim\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, let
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> be an independent Gaussian noise. Furthermore, define the time-<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> diffused marginals of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> as,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z},\qquad\mathbf{Y}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{Y}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z},\qquad\mathbf{Y}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{Y}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, by definition of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{t}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{t}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}_{t}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}_{t}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mathcal{U}_{t}\nu)\leq\mathbb{E}_{(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})}\big[\|\mathbf{X}_{t}-\mathbf{Y}_{t}\|^{2}\big]=e^{-t}\mathbb{E}_{(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})}\big[\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|^{2}\big]=e^{-t}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mathcal{U}_{t}\nu)\leq\mathbb{E}_{(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})}\big[\|\mathbf{X}_{t}-\mathbf{Y}_{t}\|^{2}\big]=e^{-t}\mathbb{E}_{(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})}\big[\|\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{Y}\|^{2}\big]=e^{-t}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the square-root yields the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We now state a property of <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> that will prove very useful when working on the limiting distribution <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> which can be expressed as a Neumann series.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Convexity of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> under mixtures)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda_{k})_{k\geq 0}\in(\mathbb{R}_{+})^{\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda_{k})_{k\geq 0}\in(\mathbb{R}_{+})^{\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> be nonnegative weights such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{k})_{k\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{k})_{k\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nu_{k})_{k\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nu_{k})_{k\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be probability measures in
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> such that the mixtures</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\mu_{k},\qquad\nu:=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\nu_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\mu_{k},\qquad\nu:=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\nu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">belong to <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)\leq\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu_{k},\nu_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)\leq\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu_{k},\nu_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}\in\Gamma(\mu_{k},\nu_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}\in\Gamma(\mu_{k},\nu_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> be an optimal coupling, so that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{k}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu_{k},\nu_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{k}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu_{k},\nu_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability measure on <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\mu_{k}=\mu,\qquad\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\nu_{k}=\nu," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\mu_{k}=\mu,\qquad\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\nu_{k}=\nu,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">meaning <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Gamma(\mu,\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Gamma(\mu,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)\leq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,\pi(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)\leq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,\pi(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using the definition of <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,\pi(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\int\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{k}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,\pi(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\int\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|^{2}\,\pi_{k}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)\leq\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu_{k},\nu_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)\leq\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\lambda_{k}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu_{k},\nu_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">which proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Neumann Series and Fixed-Point Operators</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section introduces the following fundamental proposition linking Neumann Series, and linear operators on a Banach space.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.7</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Neumann Series <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be a linear operator on a Banach space with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{T}\|&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{T}\|&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the Neumann series</span></p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I-\mathcal{T})^{-1}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\mathcal{T}^{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I-\mathcal{T})^{-1}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\mathcal{T}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">converges in operator norm.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the setting described in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the recursion</p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\mapsto\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\bigl(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\mapsto\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\bigl(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">can be rewritten as a linear fixed-point equation whose solution is expressed as a Neumann series in the operator <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Intermediate Results</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we summarize two key results that are consistently invoked in our proofs. These are specific to our setting, but fundamentally rely on the classical results stated in Section <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The first central result is the contraction property of the one-step ideal sampling operator in the error-free regime described in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Contraction of the one-step ideal sampling operator)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}:\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})\to\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}:\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})\to\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the operator that maps, to each <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> the end-point marginal of the ideal reverse diffusion (truncated at <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>) , i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}\mu=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}\mu=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction on <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d}),\mathcal{W}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d}),\mathcal{W}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, with constant <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa=\sqrt{1-\alpha}e^{-t_{0}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\sqrt{1-\alpha}e^{-t_{0}/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}\mu,\mathcal{T}\nu)\leq\sqrt{1-\alpha}e^{-t_{0}/2}\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu,\nu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}\mu,\mathcal{T}\nu)\leq\sqrt{1-\alpha}e^{-t_{0}/2}\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu,\nu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider two probability distributions <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\nu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\nu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, and denote</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\mu}:=\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu,\qquad q_{\nu}:=\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\nu." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\mu}:=\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu,\qquad q_{\nu}:=\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\nu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, by contractivity of <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition B.5 (Wasserstein contraction of OU semigroup []). ‣ B.3 Wasserstein-2 Geometry ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}\mu,\mathcal{T}\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}\mu,\mathcal{T}\nu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{W}_{2}\Big(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu\big),\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\nu\big)\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{W}_{2}\Big(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu\big),\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\nu\big)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\;\leq\;e^{-t_{0}/2}\mathcal{W}_{2}(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu,\,\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\leq\;e^{-t_{0}/2}\mathcal{W}_{2}(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu,\,\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\nu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{-t_{0}/2}\mathcal{W}_{2}(q_{\mu},q_{\nu})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{-t_{0}/2}\mathcal{W}_{2}(q_{\mu},q_{\nu}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to bound <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(q_{\mu},q_{\nu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(q_{\mu},q_{\nu})</annotation></semantics></math>. To that end, consider an optimal coupling <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> be the diagonal coupling of <math id="A3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> with itself, namely the law of <math id="A3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the coupling,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}=\alpha\lambda+(1-\alpha)\pi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}=\alpha\lambda+(1-\alpha)\pi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> has first marginal <math id="A3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and second marginal <math id="A3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(q_{\mu},q_{\nu})\leq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|_{2}^{2}\tilde{\pi}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(q_{\mu},q_{\nu})\leq\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|_{2}^{2}\tilde{\pi}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">But, by definition of <math id="A3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|_{2}^{2}\tilde{\pi}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\alpha\int\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|_{2}^{2}\lambda(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})+(1-\alpha)\int\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|_{2}^{2}\pi(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|_{2}^{2}\tilde{\pi}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\alpha\int\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|_{2}^{2}\lambda(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})+(1-\alpha)\int\|\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{y}\|_{2}^{2}\pi(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">The first term is zero, because <math id="A3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is supported on the diagonal, while the second term equals <math id="A3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal coupling between <math id="A3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(q_{\mu},q_{\nu})\leq(1-\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(q_{\mu},q_{\nu})\leq(1-\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu,\nu),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">and, equivalently, taking the square root,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(q_{\mu},q_{\nu})\leq\sqrt{1-\alpha}\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu,\nu)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(q_{\mu},q_{\nu})\leq\sqrt{1-\alpha}\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu,\nu),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">Combining with the OU contraction (<a href="#A3.E35" title="Equation 35 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix C Intermediate Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) gives the final result in (<a href="#A3.E34" title="Equation 34 ‣ Proposition C.1 (Contraction of the one-step ideal sampling operator). ‣ Appendix C Intermediate Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction, the next natural question is to ask for a characterization of its fixed points.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Fixed point of the one-step ideal sampling operator)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}:\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})\to\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}:\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})\to\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the operator that maps, to each <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> the end-point marginal of the ideal reverse diffusion (truncated at <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}\mu=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}\mu=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, any fixed point <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathrm{Id}-(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}})\mu^{\star}=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathrm{Id}-(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}})\mu^{\star}=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed point of <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{T}\mu^{\star}=\mu^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{T}\mu^{\star}=\mu^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu^{\star}\big)=\mu^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu^{\star}\big)=\mu^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(p_{\mathrm{data}})+(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\mu^{\star}\big)=\mu^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\big(p_{\mathrm{data}})+(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\mu^{\star}\big)=\mu^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\iff(\mathrm{Id}-(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}})\mu^{\star}=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\iff(\mathrm{Id}-(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}})\mu^{\star}=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second and third lines use the linearity of the sampling operator <math id="A3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Collapse distribution: existence, uniqueness, and explicit form). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(i) Limiting distribution expression</span><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}:\mu\mapsto\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}:\mu\mapsto\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>, where the operator <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in (<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Forward diffusion ‣ 2 Background ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), is the one-step ideal sampling operator in the error-free regime. By Proposition <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition C.1 (Contraction of the one-step ideal sampling operator). ‣ Appendix C Intermediate Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction on <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d}),\mathcal{W}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d}),\mathcal{W}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with constant <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa=\sqrt{(1-\alpha)}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}\;&lt;\;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\sqrt{(1-\alpha)}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}\;&lt;\;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and Banach’s fixed point theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite> gives existence and uniqueness.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, by Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition B.7 (Neumann Series []). ‣ B.4 Neumann Series and Fixed-Point Operators ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>, the Neumann series converges:
<math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathrm{Id}-(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}})^{-1}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathrm{Id}-(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}})^{-1}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the semigroup property, <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}^{k}=\mathcal{U}_{kt_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}^{k}=\mathcal{U}_{kt_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> <span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(ii)</span>), hence</p>
<table id="A4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\infty}^{\star}=(\mathrm{Id}-(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}})^{-1}\,\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\infty}^{\star}=(\mathrm{Id}-(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}})^{-1}\,\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{U}_{kt_{0}}\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{U}_{kt_{0}}\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(ii) Geometric rate of convergence</span><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N}:=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N},p_{\infty}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N}:=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N},p_{\infty}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim that <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N+1}\leq\kappa\,D_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N+1}\leq\kappa\,D_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the triangle inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N+1}=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},p_{\infty}^{\star})\leq\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},\,\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N})+\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N},\,p_{\infty}^{\star})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N+1}=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},p_{\infty}^{\star})\leq\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},\,\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N})+\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N},\,p_{\infty}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First term.</span><span id="A4.SS1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Since we are working in the error-free regime <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N+1}=\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N+1}=\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> (perfect sampler) thus <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},\,\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},\,\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Second term.</span><span id="A4.SS1.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Since <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}=\mathcal{T}p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}=\mathcal{T}p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to bound <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N},\,\mathcal{T}p_{\infty}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N},\,\mathcal{T}p_{\infty}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. Once again, the contraction property of <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition C.1 (Contraction of the one-step ideal sampling operator). ‣ Appendix C Intermediate Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>) yields,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N},\,p_{\infty}^{\star})\leq\kappa\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N},p_{\infty}^{\star})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}\hat{p}^{N},\,p_{\infty}^{\star})\leq\kappa\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N},p_{\infty}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa:=\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa:=\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining the two bounds:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N+1}\leq\kappa\,D_{N}\qquad N\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N+1}\leq\kappa\,D_{N}\qquad N\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">and iterating (<a href="#A4.E36" title="Equation 36 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) yields the geometric decay rate,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N}\leq\kappa^{N}\,D_{0}\qquad N\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N}\leq\kappa^{N}\,D_{0}\qquad N\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Proof of Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 3.2 (Limiting behaviors). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">In this proof, we use the Neumann series representation (Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Collapse distribution: existence, uniqueness, and explicit form). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>)</span></p>
<table id="A4.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">with geometric weights <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}(\alpha)=\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}(\alpha)=\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also denote <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D:=\mathcal{W}_{2}(p_{\mathrm{data}},\gamma)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D:=\mathcal{W}_{2}(p_{\mathrm{data}},\gamma)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. The proofs mainly rely on the two following facts:</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Convexity of <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> under mixtures.</span> By Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition B.6 (Convexity of 𝒲_2^2 under mixtures). ‣ B.3 Wasserstein-2 Geometry ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>, for any target distribution <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> given in (<a href="#A4.E37" title="Equation 37 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>) is a convex combination with <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}\pi_{k}(\alpha)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}\pi_{k}(\alpha)=1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},\nu)\leq\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\nu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},\nu)\leq\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\nu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Contraction of <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> on the OU sampling operator</span>. By Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Proposition B.5 (Wasserstein contraction of OU semigroup []). ‣ B.3 Wasserstein-2 Geometry ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>, for any <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, the OU sampling operator satisfies</p>
<table id="A4.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\gamma)=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mathcal{U}_{t}\gamma)\leq e^{-t/2}\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu,\gamma)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\gamma)=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu,\mathcal{U}_{t}\gamma)\leq e^{-t/2}\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu,\gamma),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant under <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(i) Limit <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Fix <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{k}:=\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{k}:=\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}=\alpha\mu_{0}+\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)\mu_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}=\alpha\mu_{0}+\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)\mu_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We can use <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{k}(\alpha)\}_{k\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{k}(\alpha)\}_{k\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> to define a natural coupling between <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}\sim p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}\sim p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}=\mathbf{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}=\mathbf{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}(\alpha)=\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}(\alpha)=\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition B.6 (Convexity of 𝒲_2^2 under mixtures). ‣ B.3 Wasserstein-2 Geometry ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> with target <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},\mu_{0})\leq\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu_{k},\mu_{0})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},\mu_{0})\leq\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(\mu_{k},\mu_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover, by the triangle inequality and (<a href="#A4.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ Item 2 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A4.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu_{k},\mu_{0})\leq\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu_{k},\gamma)+\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu_{0},\gamma)\leq e^{-(k+1)t_{0}/2}D+e^{-t_{0}/2}D\leq 2D." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>D</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu_{k},\mu_{0})\leq\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu_{k},\gamma)+\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mu_{0},\gamma)\leq e^{-(k+1)t_{0}/2}D+e^{-t_{0}/2}D\leq 2D.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore</p>
<table id="A4.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq 4D^{2}\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)=4D^{2}\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}=4D^{2}(1-\alpha)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq 4D^{2}\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)=4D^{2}\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}=4D^{2}(1-\alpha),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">which converges to zero as <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(ii) Limit <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Using (<a href="#A2.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Proposition B.6 (Convexity of 𝒲_2^2 under mixtures). ‣ B.3 Wasserstein-2 Geometry ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) with target <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and then
(<a href="#A4.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ Item 2 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\gamma\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\gamma\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq D^{2}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)e^{-(k+1)t_{0}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq D^{2}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)e^{-(k+1)t_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The geometric sum is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)e^{-(k+1)t_{0}}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}e^{-(k+1)t_{0}}=\frac{\alpha e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\pi_{k}(\alpha)e^{-(k+1)t_{0}}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}e^{-(k+1)t_{0}}=\frac{\alpha e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the denominator converges to <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-t_{0}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-t_{0}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> as
<math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</p>
<table id="A4.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},\gamma)\leq D^{2}\frac{\alpha e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}\longrightarrow 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},\gamma)\leq D^{2}\frac{\alpha e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}\longrightarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(iii) Limit <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Fix <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. By Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> <span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vii)</span>, for each fixed <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})\xrightarrow[t_{0}\to 0^{+}]{\mathcal{W}_{2}}p_{\mathrm{data}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">0</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒲</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub></munderover><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})\xrightarrow[t_{0}\to 0^{+}]{\mathcal{W}_{2}}p_{\mathrm{data}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now applying Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition B.6 (Convexity of 𝒲_2^2 under mixtures). ‣ B.3 Wasserstein-2 Geometry ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> with <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> yields,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">But by (<a href="#A4.E41" title="Equation 41 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), for each fixed <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)\xrightarrow[t_{0}\to 0^{+}]{}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">0</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.710em">+</mo></msup></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)\xrightarrow[t_{0}\to 0^{+}]{}0</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,
uniformly in <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)\leq\mathcal{W}_{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\gamma\bigr)+\mathcal{W}_{2}(\gamma,p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq 2D." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)\leq\mathcal{W}_{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\gamma\bigr)+\mathcal{W}_{2}(\gamma,p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq 2D.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus each summand in (<a href="#A4.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Proof of Corollary ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) is bounded by
<math id="A4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4D^{2}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4D^{2}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k},</annotation></semantics></math>
which is summable in <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, by dominated convergence for series, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{t_{0}\to 0}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{t_{0}\to 0}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\lim_{t_{0}\to 0}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\lim_{t_{0}\to 0}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}\lim_{t_{0}\to 0}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{k}\lim_{t_{0}\to 0}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\bigl(\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}},p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(iv) Strict positivity when <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}\neq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}\neq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
If one assumes by contradiction that <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}=p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}=p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> but since <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is characterized as a fixed
point of <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\mapsto\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\bigl(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\mapsto\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\bigl(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mu\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A4.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\bigl(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\bigl(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)p_{\mathrm{data}}\bigr)=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant under the OU transition at time <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. But, the OU semigroup has the unique invariant probability measure <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> </span><span id="A4.SS2.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(v)</span><span id="A4.SS2.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text">). Therefore <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}=\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}=\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, and this contradicts the initial assumption. Thus, <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}\neq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}\neq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Moments of limiting distribution</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Looking at the first two moments of the collapsed distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> hints at what collapse imply in terms of concentration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Moments)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mean and covariance of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> are</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{p_{\infty}^{\star}}[\mathbf{X}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{p_{\infty}^{\star}}[\mathbf{X}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}/2}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}/2}}\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}/2}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}/2}}\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\infty}^{\star}}(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\infty}^{\star}}(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}\;\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}(\mathbf{X})+\left(1-\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}\right)\mathbf{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}\;\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}(\mathbf{X})+\left(1-\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}\right)\mathbf{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mean is attenuated relative to <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the covariance is pulled toward <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Both effects are monotone in <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}\;=\;\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\,\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}\;=\;\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\,\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, recall from (<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Forward diffusion ‣ 2 Background ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) that the Ornstein-Uhlenbeck operator acts on marginals as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu:=\;\mathrm{Law}\!\Bigl(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z}\Bigr),\qquad\mathbf{X}\sim\mu,\quad\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})\text{ independent}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.782em;" width="1.782em"><mi>Law</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext> independent</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu:=\;\mathrm{Law}\!\Bigl(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\,\mathbf{Z}\Bigr),\qquad\mathbf{X}\sim\mu,\quad\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})\text{ independent}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus for any <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}_{2}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}(\mu)}[\mathbf{X}]=e^{-t/2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim\mu}[\mathbf{X}],\qquad\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbf{X}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}(\mu)}(\mathbf{X})=e^{-t}\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbf{X}\sim\mu}(\mathbf{X})+(1-e^{-t})\mathbf{I}_{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}(\mu)}[\mathbf{X}]=e^{-t/2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim\mu}[\mathbf{X}],\qquad\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbf{X}\sim\mathcal{U}_{t}(\mu)}(\mathbf{X})=e^{-t}\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbf{X}\sim\mu}(\mathbf{X})+(1-e^{-t})\mathbf{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging this in the series (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Theorem 3.1 (Collapse distribution: existence, uniqueness, and explicit form). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\infty}^{\star}}[\mathbf{X}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\infty}^{\star}}[\mathbf{X}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex73.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}_{k}\sim\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}_{k}\sim\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\,e^{-(k+1)t_{0}/2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\,e^{-(k+1)t_{0}/2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha e^{-t_{0}/2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}]\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}[e^{-t_{0}/2}(1-\alpha)]^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha e^{-t_{0}/2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}]\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}[e^{-t_{0}/2}(1-\alpha)]^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}/2}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}/2}}\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}/2}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}/2}}\;\mathbb{E}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\infty}}[\mathbf{X}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\infty}}[\mathbf{X}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\,\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbf{X}_{k}\sim\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\,\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbf{X}_{k}\sim\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\,e^{-(k+1)t_{0}}\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}]+\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}(1-e^{-(k+1)t_{0}})\mathbf{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\,e^{-(k+1)t_{0}}\mathrm{Cov}_{\mathbf{X}\sim p_{\mathrm{data}}}[\mathbf{X}]+\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}(1-e^{-(k+1)t_{0}})\mathbf{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}\;\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}(\mathbf{X})+\left(1-\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}\right)\mathbf{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Cov</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}\;\mathrm{Cov}_{p_{\mathrm{data}}}(\mathbf{X})+\left(1-\frac{\alpha\,e^{-t_{0}}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-t_{0}}}\right)\mathbf{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Spectral representation of the collapse distribution). ‣ 3.1 Spectral decomposition of the collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.I2.i4" title="Item A4 ‣ 3.1 Spectral decomposition of the collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A4</span></a>, the data distribution admits
a density <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathrm{data}}:=\frac{\mathrm{d}p_{\mathrm{data}}}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}\in L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathrm{data}}:=\frac{\mathrm{d}p_{\mathrm{data}}}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}\in L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the OU sampling operator
<math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves absolute continuity with respect to <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the collapse
distribution <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> also admits a density
<math id="A4.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\infty}^{\star}:=\frac{\mathrm{d}p_{\infty}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\infty}^{\star}:=\frac{\mathrm{d}p_{\infty}^{\star}}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Collapse distribution: existence, uniqueness, and explicit form). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we have the
Neumann-series representation</span></p>
<table id="A4.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\mathcal{U}_{(k+1)t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the OU semigroup acting on <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> (see Section <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>). By Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> </span><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vi)</span><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text">),</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}=P_{t}\!\left(\frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}=P_{t}\!\left(\frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}\gamma}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying this to (<a href="#A4.E46" title="Equation 46 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>) and using the linearity of <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\infty}^{\star}=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}P_{(k+1)t_{0}}f_{\mathrm{data}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\infty}^{\star}=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}P_{(k+1)t_{0}}f_{\mathrm{data}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">with convergence in <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathrm{data}}\in L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathrm{data}}\in L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, by Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Orthogonal Basis of 𝐿^2⁢(𝛾)). ‣ Hermite polynomials. ‣ B.2 Role of the Gaussian distribution and Decomposition in the Hermite Polynomial Basis ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a></span></p>
<table id="A4.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathrm{data}}=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}\langle f_{\mathrm{data}},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathrm{data}}=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}\langle f_{\mathrm{data}},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">with convergence in <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>. But, by Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition B.3 (Diagonalization of the OU semigroup). ‣ Hermite polynomials. ‣ B.2 Role of the Gaussian distribution and Decomposition in the Hermite Polynomial Basis ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, for each <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{(k+1)t_{0}}H_{\mathbf{n}}=e^{-|\mathbf{n}|(k+1)t_{0}/2}H_{\mathbf{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{(k+1)t_{0}}H_{\mathbf{n}}=e^{-|\mathbf{n}|(k+1)t_{0}/2}H_{\mathbf{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, applying <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{(k+1)t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{(k+1)t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and combining equations (<a href="#A4.E49" title="Equation 49 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E48" title="Equation 48 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) yields,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{(k+1)t_{0}}f_{\mathrm{data}}=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|(k+1)t_{0}/2}\langle f_{\mathrm{data}},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{(k+1)t_{0}}f_{\mathrm{data}}=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|(k+1)t_{0}/2}\langle f_{\mathrm{data}},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}H_{\mathbf{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting (<a href="#A4.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>) into (<a href="#A4.E47" title="Equation 47 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|(k+1)t_{0}/2}\langle f_{\mathrm{data}},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle H_{\mathbf{n}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|(k+1)t_{0}/2}\langle f_{\mathrm{data}},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle H_{\mathbf{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction on <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> and the coefficients are
square-summable, the series converges absolutely in <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, which
justifies exchanging the sums. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\infty}^{\star}=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}\left[\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|(k+1)t_{0}/2}\right]\langle f_{\mathrm{data}},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle H_{\mathbf{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\infty}^{\star}=\sum_{\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}}\left[\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|(k+1)t_{0}/2}\right]\langle f_{\mathrm{data}},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle H_{\mathbf{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now looking at each term inside the series on <math id="A4.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{N}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{N}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we observe that, for each <math id="A4.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}\in\mathbb{N}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|(k+1)t_{0}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{k}e^{-|\mathbf{n}|(k+1)t_{0}/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\left[(1-\alpha)e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}\right]^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\left[(1-\alpha)e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}\right]^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}\frac{1}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}}\qquad((1-\alpha)e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}&lt;1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}\frac{1}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}}\qquad((1-\alpha)e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}&lt;1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Denoting <math id="A4.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathbf{n}}(\alpha,t_{0})=\frac{\alpha e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathbf{n}}(\alpha,t_{0})=\frac{\alpha e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}}{1-(1-\alpha)e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, yields (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ Proposition 3.3 (Spectral representation of the collapse distribution). ‣ 3.1 Spectral decomposition of the collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f_{\infty}^{\star},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}=m_{\mathbf{n}}(\alpha,t_{0})\langle f_{\mathrm{data}},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f_{\infty}^{\star},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)}=m_{\mathbf{n}}(\alpha,t_{0})\langle f_{\mathrm{data}},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle_{L^{2}(\gamma)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, each Hermite mode of the data distribution is attenuated by the explicit factor <math id="A4.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathbf{n}}(\alpha,t_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathbf{n}}(\alpha,t_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. This shows that the collapse distribution is a spectrally filtered version of <math id="A4.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with preferential suppression of high-frequency modes.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Asymptotic effect of generation-dependent truncation). ‣ Generation-dependent truncation ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We consider the error-free recursion</span></p>
<table id="A4.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{i+1}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(i)}}\bigl(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{i}\bigr),\qquad i\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{i+1}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(i)}}\bigl(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{i}\bigr),\qquad i\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first prove (<a href="#S4.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Theorem 4.1 (Asymptotic effect of generation-dependent truncation). ‣ Generation-dependent truncation ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) by induction on <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math>, by linearity of <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> </span><span id="A4.SS5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(i)</span><span id="A4.SS5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text">),</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{1}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(0)}}\bigl(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{0}\bigr)=\alpha\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(0)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(0)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{1}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(0)}}\bigl(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{0}\bigr)=\alpha\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(0)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(0)}}p_{\mathrm{data}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">which agrees with (<a href="#S4.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Theorem 4.1 (Asymptotic effect of generation-dependent truncation). ‣ Generation-dependent truncation ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), since</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0,1}=t_{0}^{(0)},\qquad s_{0,1}=t_{0}^{(0)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0,1}=t_{0}^{(0)},\qquad s_{0,1}=t_{0}^{(0)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume now that (<a href="#S4.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Theorem 4.1 (Asymptotic effect of generation-dependent truncation). ‣ Generation-dependent truncation ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) holds for some <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, that is,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}=\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m}\,\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}=\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m}\,\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{m,N}=\sum_{\ell=N-1-m}^{N-1}t_{0}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{m,N}=\sum_{\ell=N-1-m}^{N-1}t_{0}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0,N}=\sum_{\ell=0}^{N-1}t_{0}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0,N}=\sum_{\ell=0}^{N-1}t_{0}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Once again, by linearity of <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and leveraging the induction assumption,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{p}^{N+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{p}^{N+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\bigl(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{N}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\bigl(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{N}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\hat{p}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\hat{p}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\!\left[\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m}\,\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}\hat{p}^{0}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\!\left[\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m}\,\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}\hat{p}^{0}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+\!\left[\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m+1}\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}\hat{p}^{0}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+\!\left[\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m+1}\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}\hat{p}^{0}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">But, by semigroup property of <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, </span><span id="A4.SS5.p3.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(ii)</span><span id="A4.SS5.p3.3.3" class="ltx_text">), <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext=",\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+\sigma_{m,N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+\sigma_{m,N}}</annotation></semantics></math> and similarly <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+s_{0,N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+s_{0,N}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Observing that <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(N)}+\sigma_{m,N}=\sum_{\ell=N-m}^{N}t_{0}^{(\ell)}=\sigma_{m+1,N+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(N)}+\sigma_{m,N}=\sum_{\ell=N-m}^{N}t_{0}^{(\ell)}=\sigma_{m+1,N+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(N)}+s_{0,N}=s_{0,N+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(N)}+s_{0,N}=s_{0,N+1}</annotation></semantics></math> finally yields,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N+1}=\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N}(1-\alpha)^{m}\,\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N+1}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N+1}}p_{\mathrm{data}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N+1}=\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N}(1-\alpha)^{m}\,\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N+1}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N+1}}p_{\mathrm{data}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is exactly (<a href="#S4.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Theorem 4.1 (Asymptotic effect of generation-dependent truncation). ‣ Generation-dependent truncation ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) with <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N+1</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves the
representation formula for all <math id="A4.SS5.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Asymptotic behavior when <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(i)}\to t_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(i)}\to t_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Assume that <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(i)}\to t_{\infty}\in[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(i)}\to t_{\infty}\in[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the geometric weights <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{m}(\alpha)=\alpha(1-\alpha)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{m}(\alpha)=\alpha(1-\alpha)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <span id="A4.SS5.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">annealed truncation limiting distribution</span> <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}</annotation></semantics></math> as,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}:=\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}:=\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The objective of this part is to show that <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N},p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})})\underset{N\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N},p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})})\underset{N\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}0</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that, for any fixed <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{m,N}:=\sum_{\ell=N-1-m}^{N-1}t_{0}^{(\ell)}\,\longrightarrow\,(m+1)t_{\infty}\quad\text{as }N\to\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em" stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{m,N}:=\sum_{\ell=N-1-m}^{N-1}t_{0}^{(\ell)}\,\longrightarrow\,(m+1)t_{\infty}\quad\text{as }N\to\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p4.3" class="ltx_p">By continuity of <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto\mathcal{U}_{t}(p_{\mathrm{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto\mathcal{U}_{t}(p_{\mathrm{data}})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, <span id="A4.SS5.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vii)</span>),</p>
<table id="A4.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})\;\xrightarrow[N\to\infty]{\mathcal{W}_{2}}\;\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})\qquad\text{for each fixed }m." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒲</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub></munderover><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for each fixed </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})\;\xrightarrow[N\to\infty]{\mathcal{W}_{2}}\;\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})\qquad\text{for each fixed }m.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p4.4" class="ltx_p">We now compare <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}</annotation></semantics></math> as mixtures with the
same total weights. To that end, we decompose <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}=\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})+(1-\alpha)^{N}r_{N}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}=\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})+(1-\alpha)^{N}r_{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p4.5" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A4.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{N}:=\frac{1}{(1-\alpha)^{N}}\sum_{m=N}^{\infty}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}=\alpha\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{j}\mathcal{U}_{(N+j+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{N}:=\frac{1}{(1-\alpha)^{N}}\sum_{m=N}^{\infty}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}=\alpha\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{j}\mathcal{U}_{(N+j+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p4.6" class="ltx_p">The measure <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability measure. By convexity of <math id="A4.SS5.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> under mixtures (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition B.6 (Convexity of 𝒲_2^2 under mixtures). ‣ B.3 Wasserstein-2 Geometry ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A4.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\hat{p}^{N},p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\hat{p}^{N},p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}\right)+(1-\alpha)^{N}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}},r_{N}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}\right)+(1-\alpha)^{N}\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}},r_{N}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We treat the two terms separately.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First term.</span><span id="A4.SS5.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Fix <math id="A4.SS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex95.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{m=0}^{M}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{m=0}^{M}\pi_{m}(\alpha)\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}},\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{m=M+1}^{N-1}\pi_{m}(\alpha)B," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{m=M+1}^{N-1}\pi_{m}(\alpha)B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> is a uniform second-moment bound. Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> </span><span id="A4.SS5.p6.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(iv)</span><span id="A4.SS5.p6.2.3" class="ltx_text"> ensures that, for any <math id="A4.SS5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> has uniformly bounded second moment,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{t\geq 0}\int\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}_{2}\,\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})\leq\int\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}_{2}\,p_{\mathrm{data}}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})+d," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{t\geq 0}\int\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}_{2}\,\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})\leq\int\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}_{2}\,p_{\mathrm{data}}(\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x})+d,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, all the above pairwise <math id="A4.SS5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-distances are bounded uniformly.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For fixed <math id="A4.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, the finite sum converges to zero by the continuity invoked in (<a href="#A4.E55" title="Equation 55 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>). The tail satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=M+1}^{N-1}\pi_{m}(\alpha)B=B\sum_{m=M+1}^{N-1}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=M+1}^{N-1}\pi_{m}(\alpha)B=B\sum_{m=M+1}^{N-1}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex97.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq B\sum_{m=M+1}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq B\sum_{m=M+1}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=B(1-\alpha)^{M+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=B(1-\alpha)^{M+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">which can be made arbitrarily small by choosing <math id="A4.SS5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> large. Hence the first term in (<a href="#A4.E56" title="Equation 56 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) converges to zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Second term.</span><span id="A4.SS5.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text"> For the second term in (<a href="#A4.E56" title="Equation 56 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>), as stated in (<a href="#A4.E57" title="Equation 57 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>), <math id="A4.SS5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> has uniformly bounded second moments by Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> </span><span id="A4.SS5.p8.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(iv)</span><span id="A4.SS5.p8.1.4" class="ltx_text">. As <math id="A4.SS5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex combination of measures of the form <math id="A4.SS5.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t_{j}}p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t_{j}}p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS5.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, its second moment is also bounded. Therefore, there exists a constant <math id="A4.SS5.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> such that,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}(\hat{p}^{0}),r_{N}\right)\leq B_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}^{2}\!\left(\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}(\hat{p}^{0}),r_{N}\right)\leq B_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A4.SS5.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.SS5.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)^{N}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)^{N}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the second term in
(<a href="#A4.E56" title="Equation 56 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) also converges to zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the two estimates yields the desired convergence</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}\!\left(\hat{p}^{N},p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}\right)\to 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}\!\left(\hat{p}^{N},p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})}\right)\to 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case </span><math id="A4.SS5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\infty}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\infty}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.SS5.p10.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span><span id="A4.SS5.p10.1.3" class="ltx_text">
If <math id="A4.SS5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\infty}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\infty}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.SS5.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}=\mathcal{U}_{0}=\mathrm{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Id</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{(m+1)t_{\infty}}=\mathcal{U}_{0}=\mathrm{Id}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A4.SS5.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{(0)}=\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{m}\,p_{\mathrm{data}}=p_{\mathrm{data}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{(0)}=\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}(1-\alpha)^{m}\,p_{\mathrm{data}}=p_{\mathrm{data}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A4.SS5.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{m}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\alpha(1-\alpha)^{m}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. This proves that the recursive
compounding effect disappears asymptotically when <math id="A4.SS5.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(i)}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(i)}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Geometric convergence and stability). ‣ Concentration around 𝑝_∞^⋆ ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof proceeds in three steps: a one-step recursion, its iteration by induction, and verification of the three regimes.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(a) One-step Recursion.</span><span id="A4.SS6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the triangle inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N+1}=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},p_{\infty}^{\star})\leq\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},\,\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}))+\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}),\,p_{\infty}^{\star})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N+1}=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},p_{\infty}^{\star})\leq\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},\,\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}))+\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}),\,p_{\infty}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the first term: since <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N+1}=\hat{\mathcal{S}}_{N}(q_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N+1}=\hat{\mathcal{S}}_{N}(q_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> (imperfect sampler) and <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N})=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N})=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> (ideal sampler applied to the same training mixture <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>), the definition of <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S5.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Score Estimation and Discretization Errors ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},\,\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}))=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{\mathcal{S}}_{N}(q_{N}),\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{N}))\leq\delta_{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{p}^{N+1},\,\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}))=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\hat{\mathcal{S}}_{N}(q_{N}),\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{N}))\leq\delta_{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">For the second term: since <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}=\mathcal{T}(p_{\infty}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}=\mathcal{T}(p_{\infty}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to bound <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}),\,\mathcal{T}(p_{\infty}^{\star}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}),\,\mathcal{T}(p_{\infty}^{\star}))</annotation></semantics></math>. But <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction (Proposition <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition C.1 (Contraction of the one-step ideal sampling operator). ‣ Appendix C Intermediate Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>) thus,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}),\,p_{\infty}^{\star})=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}),\,\mathcal{T}(p_{\infty}^{\star}))\leq\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}\;D_{N}=\kappa\,D_{N}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}),\,p_{\infty}^{\star})=\mathcal{W}_{2}(\mathcal{T}(\hat{p}^{N}),\,\mathcal{T}(p_{\infty}^{\star}))\leq\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}\;D_{N}=\kappa\,D_{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa:=\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa:=\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining the two bounds:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N+1}\leq\kappa\,D_{N}+\delta_{N},\qquad N\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N+1}\leq\kappa\,D_{N}+\delta_{N},\qquad N\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(b) Full Induction.</span><span id="A4.SS6.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove (<a href="#S5.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Theorem 5.2 (Geometric convergence and stability). ‣ Concentration around 𝑝_∞^⋆ ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) by induction on <math id="A4.SS6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. The base case <math id="A4.SS6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math> follows directly from (<a href="#A4.E58" title="Equation 58 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.6 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>): <math id="A4.SS6.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}\leq\kappa\,D_{0}+\delta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}\leq\kappa\,D_{0}+\delta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume the bound holds at generation <math id="A4.SS6.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N}\leq\kappa^{N}\,D_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}\,\delta_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N}\leq\kappa^{N}\,D_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}\,\delta_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, substituting into (<a href="#A4.E58" title="Equation 58 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.6 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{N+1}\leq\kappa\,D_{N}+\delta_{N}\leq\kappa\Bigl(\kappa^{N}\,D_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}\,\delta_{i}\Bigr)+\delta_{N}=\kappa^{N+1}\,D_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{N}\kappa^{N-i}\,\delta_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{N+1}\leq\kappa\,D_{N}+\delta_{N}\leq\kappa\Bigl(\kappa^{N}\,D_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}\,\delta_{i}\Bigr)+\delta_{N}=\kappa^{N+1}\,D_{0}+\sum_{i=0}^{N}\kappa^{N-i}\,\delta_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the induction and establishes (<a href="#S5.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Theorem 5.2 (Geometric convergence and stability). ‣ Concentration around 𝑝_∞^⋆ ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now prove the two asymptotic regimes of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Geometric convergence and stability). ‣ Concentration around 𝑝_∞^⋆ ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(i) Summable perturbations.</span>
Assume <math id="A4.SS6.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\geq 0}\delta_{i}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\geq 0}\delta_{i}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A4.SS6.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{N}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{N}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.SS6.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. The first term <math id="A4.SS6.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{N}\,D_{0}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{N}\,D_{0}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. For the convolution term, fix <math id="A4.SS6.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and choose <math id="A4.SS6.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS6.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=M}^{\infty}\delta_{i}&lt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=M}^{\infty}\delta_{i}&lt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A4.SS6.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;M</annotation></semantics></math>, split:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}\,\delta_{i}=\underbrace{\sum_{i=0}^{M-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}\,\delta_{i}}_{\to\,0\text{ as }N\to\infty\text{ ($M$ fixed, $\kappa&lt;1$)}}+\underbrace{\sum_{i=M}^{N-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}\,\delta_{i}}_{\leq\,\sum_{i=M}^{N-1}\delta_{i}\;\leq\;\sum_{i=M}^{\infty}\delta_{i}\,&lt;\,\varepsilon}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> (</mtext><mi mathsize="0.700em">M</mi><mtext> fixed, </mtext><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">κ</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">&lt;</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.448em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}\,\delta_{i}=\underbrace{\sum_{i=0}^{M-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}\,\delta_{i}}_{\to\,0\text{ as }N\to\infty\text{ ($M$ fixed, $\kappa&lt;1$)}}+\underbrace{\sum_{i=M}^{N-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}\,\delta_{i}}_{\leq\,\sum_{i=M}^{N-1}\delta_{i}\;\leq\;\sum_{i=M}^{\infty}\delta_{i}\,&lt;\,\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SS6.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrary, <math id="A4.SS6.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(ii) Constant perturbation floor.</span>
If <math id="A4.SS6.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}&lt;\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}&lt;\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the geometric sum evaluates to
<math id="A4.SS6.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}=\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\kappa^{j}=(1-\kappa^{N})/(1-\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}\kappa^{N-1-i}=\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}\kappa^{j}=(1-\kappa^{N})/(1-\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>,
so</p>
<table id="A4.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{N}\leq\kappa^{N}\,D_{0}+\frac{\delta\,(1-\kappa^{N})}{1-\kappa}\;\xrightarrow{N\to\infty}\;\frac{\delta}{1-\kappa}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.558em">→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mover><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{N}\leq\kappa^{N}\,D_{0}+\frac{\delta\,(1-\kappa^{N})}{1-\kappa}\;\xrightarrow{N\to\infty}\;\frac{\delta}{1-\kappa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p8.2" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.7 </span>Explicit characterization of perturbation</h3>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Linear perturbation recursion)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define the perturbation <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{N}:=\hat{p}^{N}-p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{N}:=\hat{p}^{N}-p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and, for each generation <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}\;:=\;\hat{p}^{i+1}-\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}\;:=\;\hat{p}^{i+1}-\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> be the <em id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">one-step perturbation</em> at generation <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the imperfect distribution <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}\;=\;p_{\infty}^{\star}\;+\;\underbrace{(1-\alpha)^{N}\,\mathcal{U}_{Nt_{0}}(\xi_{0})}_{\text{initialization transient}}\;+\;\underbrace{\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{N-1-i}\,\mathcal{U}_{(N-1-i)t_{0}}(\eta_{i})}_{\text{accumulated perturbations}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">initialization transient</mtext></munder><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">accumulated perturbations</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}\;=\;p_{\infty}^{\star}\;+\;\underbrace{(1-\alpha)^{N}\,\mathcal{U}_{Nt_{0}}(\xi_{0})}_{\text{initialization transient}}\;+\;\underbrace{\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{N-1-i}\,\mathcal{U}_{(N-1-i)t_{0}}(\eta_{i})}_{\text{accumulated perturbations}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the perturbation <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{N}:=\hat{p}^{N}-p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{N}:=\hat{p}^{N}-p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. We first prove it satisfies the following linear recursion:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{N+1}\;=\;(1-\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\xi_{N})\;+\;\eta_{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{N+1}\;=\;(1-\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\xi_{N})\;+\;\eta_{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, by definition of <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N+1}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{N})+\eta_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N+1}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{N})+\eta_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)p_{\infty}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)p_{\infty}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, subtracting and using the linearity of <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> on signed measures, we obtain the following:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi_{N+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi_{N+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex109.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\hat{p}^{N+1}-p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\hat{p}^{N+1}-p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{N})-\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)p_{\infty}^{\star})+\eta_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{N})-\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)p_{\infty}^{\star})+\eta_{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{N})-\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)p_{\infty}^{\star})+\eta_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{N})-\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\alpha\,p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)p_{\infty}^{\star})+\eta_{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})+(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\hat{p}^{N})-\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})-(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\infty}^{\star})+\eta_{N}\qquad\text{ by linearity of }\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mtext> by linearity of </mtext><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})+(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\hat{p}^{N})-\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\mathrm{data}})-(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(p_{\infty}^{\star})+\eta_{N}\qquad\text{ by linearity of }\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\!\bigl((1-\alpha)(\hat{p}^{N}-p_{\infty}^{\star})\bigr)+\eta_{N}\qquad\text{ by linearity of }\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mtext> by linearity of </mtext><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}\!\bigl((1-\alpha)(\hat{p}^{N}-p_{\infty}^{\star})\bigr)+\eta_{N}\qquad\text{ by linearity of }\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\xi_{N})+\eta_{N}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\alpha)\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\xi_{N})+\eta_{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Unrolling the recursion and applying the semigroup property <math id="A4.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}^{k}=\mathcal{U}_{kt_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}^{k}=\mathcal{U}_{kt_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> yields the end result:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}\;=\;p_{\infty}^{\star}\;+\;(1-\alpha)^{N}\,\mathcal{U}_{Nt_{0}}(\xi_{0})\;+\;\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{N-1-i}\,\mathcal{U}_{(N-1-i)t_{0}}(\eta_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}\;=\;p_{\infty}^{\star}\;+\;(1-\alpha)^{N}\,\mathcal{U}_{Nt_{0}}(\xi_{0})\;+\;\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{N-1-i}\,\mathcal{U}_{(N-1-i)t_{0}}(\eta_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS7.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS7.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Equation (<a href="#A4.E59" title="Equation 59 ‣ Proposition D.2 (Linear perturbation recursion). ‣ D.7 Explicit characterization of perturbation ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>) reveals that each iterate
<math id="A4.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> decomposes as <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> plus two correction terms. The
initialization transient decays geometrically <em id="A4.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">and</em> is progressively smoothed by <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Nt_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Nt_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> units of OU evolution. Each perturbation <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> introduced at generation <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is subsequently
smoothed by <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N{-}1{-}i)t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N{-}1{-}i)t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> units of OU evolution before being
observed at generation <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, with amplitude damped by <math id="A4.SS7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1{-}\alpha)^{N-1-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1{-}\alpha)^{N-1-i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.8 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 5.3 (Mode-dependent error propagation). ‣ Spectral Decomposition in the Learned Regime ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">In Proposition <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition D.2 (Linear perturbation recursion). ‣ D.7 Explicit characterization of perturbation ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, we explicitly wrote <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> in presence of errors as,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}\;=\;p_{\infty}^{\star}\;+\;(1-\alpha)^{N}\,\mathcal{U}_{Nt_{0}}(\xi_{0})\;+\;\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{N-1-i}\,\mathcal{U}_{(N-1-i)t_{0}}(\eta_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}\;=\;p_{\infty}^{\star}\;+\;(1-\alpha)^{N}\,\mathcal{U}_{Nt_{0}}(\xi_{0})\;+\;\sum_{i=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{N-1-i}\,\mathcal{U}_{(N-1-i)t_{0}}(\eta_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{N}=\hat{p}^{N}-p_{\infty}^{\star},\quad\text{ and }\quad\eta_{N}=\hat{p}^{N+1}-\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{N})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{N}=\hat{p}^{N}-p_{\infty}^{\star},\quad\text{ and }\quad\eta_{N}=\hat{p}^{N+1}-\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(q_{N}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS8.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now, projecting perturbation <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> onto the Hermite polynomials basis <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\mathbf{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathbf{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> acts on mode <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐧</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}</annotation></semantics></math> by multiplication by <math id="A4.SS8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition Prop. <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition B.4. ‣ Hermite polynomials. ‣ B.2 Role of the Gaussian distribution and Decomposition in the Hermite Polynomial Basis ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\xi_{N+1},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\xi_{N+1},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex118.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\xi_{N})+\eta_{N},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}(\xi_{N})+\eta_{N},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\alpha)\,e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}\,\langle\xi_{N},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle+\langle\eta_{N},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\alpha)\,e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}\,\langle\xi_{N},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle+\langle\eta_{N},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\kappa_{\mathbf{n}}\,\langle\xi_{N},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle+\langle\eta_{N},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\kappa_{\mathbf{n}}\,\langle\xi_{N},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle+\langle\eta_{N},H_{\mathbf{n}}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS8.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS8.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Unrolling gives (<a href="#S5.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ Proposition 5.3 (Mode-dependent error propagation). ‣ Spectral Decomposition in the Learned Regime ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we investigate the well-posedness of annealed truncation schedules, which consists in considering adaptive truncation times <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> that converge to <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> as the generation <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Fisher Information Instability and Properties</h3>

<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Instability of the reverse diffusion around <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first formally state the instability problem that arises near the reverse diffusion endpoint <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that, in order to sample from the reverse diffusion, one needs to estimate the score of the reverse time-<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> marginal at all times <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. For a target distribution <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> at generation <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote the score of the reverse time-<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> marginal by <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log q_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log q_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The key quantity that captures how hard these are to estimate is the Fisher information of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>, defined as the expected squared magnitude of the score:</p>
<table id="A5.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(q_{i,t})=\int\|\nabla\log q_{i,t}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}^{2}\,q_{i,t}(\mathbf{x})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(q_{i,t})=\int\|\nabla\log q_{i,t}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}^{2}\,q_{i,t}(\mathbf{x})\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In diffusion training, the score matching objective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite> at generation <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> contains terms of the form,</p>
<table id="A5.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim q_{i,t}}\big[\|\mathbf{s}_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}_{t},t)-\nabla\log q_{i,t}(\mathbf{X}_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}_{t}\sim q_{i,t}}\big[\|\mathbf{s}_{\theta}(\mathbf{X}_{t},t)-\nabla\log q_{i,t}(\mathbf{X}_{t})\|_{2}^{2}\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">suggesting that if <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(q_{i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(q_{i,t})</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#A5.E61" title="Equation 61 ‣ Instability of the reverse diffusion around 𝑡↓0 ‣ E.1 Fisher Information Instability and Properties ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>) is large, the target score itself (<a href="#A5.E62" title="Equation 62 ‣ Instability of the reverse diffusion around 𝑡↓0 ‣ E.1 Fisher Information Instability and Properties ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>) has large <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Concretely, for OU diffusion, one has</p>
<table id="A5.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}q_{i}=\mathrm{Law}(\mathbf{X}_{t}^{i})=\mathrm{Law}(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}_{0}^{i}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Law</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Law</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}q_{i}=\mathrm{Law}(\mathbf{X}_{t}^{i})=\mathrm{Law}(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}_{0}^{i}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{0}^{i}\sim q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{0}^{i}\sim q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> approaches the raw data distribution <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. If the training distribution is empirical, singular, sharp, multimodal or concentrated near a low-dimensional set, then its density develops steep gradients at small <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. The generic Fisher bound captures exactly this ((ii) in Proposition <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition E.1 (Fisher control for OU smoothing). ‣ Instability of the reverse diffusion around 𝑡↓0 ‣ E.1 Fisher Information Instability and Properties ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>) :</p>
<table id="A5.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathcal{U}_{t}q_{i})\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-t}}\underset{t\to 0}{\sim}\frac{d}{t},\qquad\text{ since }1-e^{-t}\underset{t\to 0}{\sim}t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> since </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathcal{U}_{t}q_{i})\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-t}}\underset{t\to 0}{\sim}\frac{d}{t},\qquad\text{ since }1-e^{-t}\underset{t\to 0}{\sim}t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Fisher control for OU smoothing)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> be absolutely continuous with respect to the
Lebesgue measure on <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> its Fisher information,</span></p>
<table id="A5.E63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mu)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\nabla\log\mu(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}\mu(\mathbf{x})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\frac{\|\nabla\mu(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}}{\mu(\mathbf{x})}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mu)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\nabla\log\mu(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}\mu(\mathbf{x})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\frac{\|\nabla\mu(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}}{\mu(\mathbf{x})}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We equivalently write <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math> to denote <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{U}_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the OU sampling operator (defined in (<a href="#A2.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>))
Then the following properties hold.</span></p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Quadratic scaling under dilation.</span><span id="A5.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For any </span><math id="A5.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(a\mathbf{X})=a^{-2}J(\mathbf{X})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(a\mathbf{X})=a^{-2}J(\mathbf{X}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Universal OU smoothing bound.</span><span id="A5.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For every </span><math id="A5.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iii)</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Fisher control under OU evolution.</span><span id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
If </span><math id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mu)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mu)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then for every </span><math id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)\leq e^{t}J(\mu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)\leq e^{t}J(\mu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, for </span><math id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in a bounded interval </span><math id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.ix3.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{0\leq t\leq T}J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)\leq e^{T}J(\mu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{0\leq t\leq T}J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)\leq e^{T}J(\mu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(iv)</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Convexity under mixtures.</span><span id="A5.I1.ix4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let </span><math id="A5.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1},\ldots,\mu_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1},\ldots,\mu_{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.ix4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> have smooth positive densities, and let
</span><math id="A5.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1},\ldots,w_{N}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1},\ldots,w_{N}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.ix4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfy </span><math id="A5.I1.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I1.ix4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\left(\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\mu_{k}\right)\leq\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}J(\mu_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\left(\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\mu_{k}\right)\leq\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}J(\mu_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These results are standard, and detailed proofs can be found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>. We provide proofs for completeness.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(i) Quadratic scaling under dilation.</span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}=a\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}=a\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> has density <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> has
density</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{a}(\mathbf{y})=|a|^{-d}\mu(\mathbf{y}/a)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{a}(\mathbf{y})=|a|^{-d}\mu(\mathbf{y}/a).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{y}}\log\mu_{a}(\mathbf{y})=\nabla_{\mathbf{y}}\log\mu(\mathbf{y}/a)=a^{-1}\nabla\log\mu(\mathbf{y}/a)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{y}}\log\mu_{a}(\mathbf{y})=\nabla_{\mathbf{y}}\log\mu(\mathbf{y}/a)=a^{-1}\nabla\log\mu(\mathbf{y}/a).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A5.E64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\mathbf{Y})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\nabla\log\mu_{a}(\mathbf{y})\|^{2}\mu_{a}(\mathbf{y})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left\|a^{-1}\nabla\log\mu(\mathbf{y}/a)\right\|^{2}|a|^{-d}\mu(\mathbf{y}/a)\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathbf{Y})=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\nabla\log\mu_{a}(\mathbf{y})\|^{2}\mu_{a}(\mathbf{y})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\left\|a^{-1}\nabla\log\mu(\mathbf{y}/a)\right\|^{2}|a|^{-d}\mu(\mathbf{y}/a)\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">By change of variables <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}=a\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}=a\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#A5.E64" title="Equation 64 ‣ Proof. ‣ Instability of the reverse diffusion around 𝑡↓0 ‣ E.1 Fisher Information Instability and Properties ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>) yields the desired results:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathbf{Y})=a^{-2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\nabla\log\mu(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}\mu(\mathbf{x})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=a^{-2}J(\mathbf{X})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathbf{Y})=a^{-2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\|\nabla\log\mu(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}\mu(\mathbf{x})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=a^{-2}J(\mathbf{X}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(ii) Universal OU smoothing bound.</span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Fix <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{Y}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim\mu\perp\!\!\!\perp\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mpadded style="width:0.518em;" width="0.518em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim\mu\perp\!\!\!\perp\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}=1-e^{-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}=1-e^{-t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the standard Fisher-information inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathbf{X}_{1}+\mathbf{X}_{2})\leq J(\mathbf{X}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathbf{X}_{1}+\mathbf{X}_{2})\leq J(\mathbf{X}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for any two independent random variables <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{1}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{1}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{2}=\sigma_{t}\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{2}=\sigma_{t}\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> gives,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathbf{Y}_{t})\leq J(\sigma_{t}\mathbf{Z})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathbf{Y}_{t})\leq J(\sigma_{t}\mathbf{Z}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}\mathbf{Z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, its Fisher information is</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\sigma_{t}\mathbf{Z})=\frac{d}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}=\frac{d}{1-e^{-t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\sigma_{t}\mathbf{Z})=\frac{d}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}=\frac{d}{1-e^{-t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)=J(\mathbf{Y}_{t})\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)=J(\mathbf{Y}_{t})\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(iii) Fisher control under OU evolution.</span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Once again, let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as
<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{Y}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}_{t}=e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}+\sqrt{1-e^{-t}}\mathbf{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the same monotonicity property Fisher information used in </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(ii)</span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text">,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\mathbf{Y}_{t})\leq J(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathbf{Y}_{t})\leq J(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the scaling property proved in </span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(i)</span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.3" class="ltx_text"> with <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a=e^{-t/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=e^{-t/2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X})=e^{t}J(\mathbf{X})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(e^{-t/2}\mathbf{X})=e^{t}J(\mathbf{X}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)=J(\mathbf{Y}_{t})\leq e^{t}J(\mu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)=J(\mathbf{Y}_{t})\leq e^{t}J(\mu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{t}\leq e^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{t}\leq e^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{0\leq t\leq T}J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)\leq e^{T}J(\mu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{0\leq t\leq T}J(\mathcal{U}_{t}\mu)\leq e^{T}J(\mu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(iv) Convexity under mixtures.</span><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text">
Let <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1},\ldots,\mu_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1},\ldots,\mu_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> denote both the probability measures and their smooth
positive densities and define the convex mixture distribution <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\mu_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\mu_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by taking the gradient of <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex138" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla\mu=\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\nabla\mu_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mu=\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\nabla\mu_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Noticing that the map <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,\mathbf{v})\mapsto\frac{\|\mathbf{v}\|^{2}}{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>u</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,\mathbf{v})\mapsto\frac{\|\mathbf{v}\|^{2}}{u}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex, one has pointwise in <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\|\nabla\mu(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}}{\mu(\mathbf{x})}=\frac{\left\|\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\nabla\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})\right\|^{2}}{\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})}\leq\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\frac{\|\nabla\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}}{\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>‖</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\|\nabla\mu(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}}{\mu(\mathbf{x})}=\frac{\left\|\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\nabla\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})\right\|^{2}}{\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})}\leq\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\frac{\|\nabla\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}}{\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Integrating over <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the final result,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mu)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\frac{\|\nabla\mu(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}}{\mu(\mathbf{x})}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}\leq\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\frac{\|\nabla\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}}{\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}J(\mu_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mu)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\frac{\|\nabla\mu(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}}{\mu(\mathbf{x})}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}\leq\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\frac{\|\nabla\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})\|^{2}}{\mu_{k}(\mathbf{x})}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{x}=\sum_{k=1}^{N}w_{k}J(\mu_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Annealed Truncation</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The instability of score estimation near <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> highlights the limits of considering truncation times <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> that tend to zero. The recursive structure partially mitigates this problem, because synthetic samples have already passed through previous OU smoothing steps. However, it does not imply that the whole synthetic distribution has accumulated the full cumulative smoothing <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j&lt;i}t_{0}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j&lt;i}t_{0}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> since, in our setting, fresh-data are reintroduced at each generation, and recently injected components have only been smoothed for the most recent truncation times. The following decomposition makes this precise.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Fisher decomposition under annealed truncation)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the error-free annealed recursion with schedules <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{0}^{(i)})_{i\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{0}^{(i)})_{i\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.E65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{i+1}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(i)}}\bigl(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{i}\bigr),\qquad\hat{p}^{0}=p_{\mathrm{data}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{i+1}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(i)}}\bigl(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{i}\bigr),\qquad\hat{p}^{0}=p_{\mathrm{data}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(i)}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(i)}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for each generation <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.E66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}J(q_{N,t_{0}^{(N)}})&amp;\leq\alpha J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}})+(1-\alpha)\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}})\\
&amp;\qquad+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}),\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}J(q_{N,t_{0}^{(N)}})&amp;\leq\alpha J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}})+(1-\alpha)\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}})\\
&amp;\qquad+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{m,N}:=\sum_{\ell=0}^{N-1}t_{0}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{m,N}:=\sum_{\ell=0}^{N-1}t_{0}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0,N}:=\sum_{\ell=0}^{N-1}t_{0}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0,N}:=\sum_{\ell=0}^{N-1}t_{0}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Asymptotic effect of generation-dependent truncation). ‣ Generation-dependent truncation ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, for any finite horizon <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A5.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}=\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m}\,\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}=\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m}\,\mathcal{U}_{\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N}\mathcal{U}_{s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[t_{0}^{(i)},T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[t_{0}^{(i)},T]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{N,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{N,t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{N,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{N,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex141.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{U}_{t}(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{N})=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t}\hat{p}^{N}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{U}_{t}(\alpha p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\hat{p}^{N})=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t}\hat{p}^{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we have used the linearity of <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>).
Thus, plugging the expression of <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> given in (<a href="#A5.E67" title="Equation 67 ‣ Proof. ‣ E.2 Annealed Truncation ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>) and using linearity again, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{N,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{N,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex142.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t}\hat{p}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)\mathcal{U}_{t}\hat{p}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}+\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m+1}\mathcal{U}_{t+\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}\mathcal{U}_{t+s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}+\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m+1}\mathcal{U}_{t+\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}\mathcal{U}_{t+s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">The Fisher bound (<a href="#A5.E66" title="Equation 66 ‣ Proposition E.2 (Fisher decomposition under annealed truncation). ‣ E.2 Annealed Truncation ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>) follows from (<a href="#A5.Ex142" title="In Proof. ‣ E.2 Annealed Truncation ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>) using the convexity of Fisher information under mixtures (Proposition (iv) <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition E.1 (Fisher control for OU smoothing). ‣ Instability of the reverse diffusion around 𝑡↓0 ‣ E.1 Fisher Information Instability and Properties ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>) and taking <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=t_{0}^{(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=t_{0}^{(N)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition E.2 (Fisher decomposition under annealed truncation). ‣ E.2 Annealed Truncation ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> clearly differentiates between two terms. On the one hand, components injected many generations in the past have accumulated several steps of smoothing and are regularized by the recursion. On the other hand, components injected more recently have less smoothing, and the fresh component
<math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t}p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> has only been smoothed by the current truncation time <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(N)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, recursive self-regularization does not by itself give a uniform Fisher bound as <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\downarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\downarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> for arbitrary raw data. We distinguish the settings in which these annealed truncations are well-defined.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.2.1 </span>Case 1: Fresh-data proportion <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and finite Fisher information</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If the unknown target distribution <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> has finite Fisher information, then annealed truncation schedules are well-defined.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary E.3</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Annealing under finite-Fisher regularity)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> has finite Fisher information, i.e. if <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, then, for a bounded positive truncation schedule <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{0}^{(N)})_{N\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{0}^{(N)})_{N\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{N}J\bigl(q_{N,t_{0}^{(N)}}\bigr)&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>N</mi></munder><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{N}J\bigl(q_{N,t_{0}^{(N)}}\bigr)&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}:=\sup_{N}t_{0}^{(N)}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>N</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}:=\sup_{N}t_{0}^{(N)}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. By
(<a href="#A5.Ex142" title="In Proof. ‣ E.2 Annealed Truncation ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>), evaluated at <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=t_{0}^{(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=t_{0}^{(N)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{N,t_{0}^{(N)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{N,t_{0}^{(N)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex144.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m+1}\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m+1}\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">The coefficients in this decomposition are non-negative and sum to one. Hence, by
convexity of Fisher information under mixtures,</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(q_{N,t_{0}^{(N)}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(q_{N,t_{0}^{(N)}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex145.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\alpha J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}})+\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m+1}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\alpha J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}p_{\mathrm{data}})+\alpha\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}(1-\alpha)^{m+1}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+\sigma_{m,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+(1-\alpha)^{N+1}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}+s_{0,N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now show that every term appearing on the right-hand side is uniformly
bounded. Since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, Proposition <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition E.1 (Fisher control for OU smoothing). ‣ Instability of the reverse diffusion around 𝑡↓0 ‣ E.1 Fisher Information Instability and Properties ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>(iii) implies that, for <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq s\leq T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq s\leq T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathcal{U}_{s}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq e^{T_{0}}J(p_{\mathrm{data}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathcal{U}_{s}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq e^{T_{0}}J(p_{\mathrm{data}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, for <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq T_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq T_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, Proposition <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition E.1 (Fisher control for OU smoothing). ‣ Instability of the reverse diffusion around 𝑡↓0 ‣ E.1 Fisher Information Instability and Properties ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>(ii) gives the universal smoothing bound</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex147" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathcal{U}_{s}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-s}}\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-T_{0}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathcal{U}_{s}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-s}}\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-T_{0}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, for all <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathcal{U}_{s}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq C_{T_{0},p_{\mathrm{data}}}:=\max\left\{e^{T_{0}}J(p_{\mathrm{data}}),\frac{d}{1-e^{-T_{0}}}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathcal{U}_{s}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq C_{T_{0},p_{\mathrm{data}}}:=\max\left\{e^{T_{0}}J(p_{\mathrm{data}}),\frac{d}{1-e^{-T_{0}}}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Applying this bound to each component in the convex decomposition (<a href="#A5.Ex145" title="In Proof. ‣ E.2.1 Case 1: Fresh-data proportion 𝛼&gt;0 and finite Fisher information ‣ E.2 Annealed Truncation ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(q_{N,t_{0}^{(N)}})\leq C_{T_{0},p_{\mathrm{data}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(q_{N,t_{0}^{(N)}})\leq C_{T_{0},p_{\mathrm{data}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">for every <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark E.4</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Interpretation of the finite Fisher information assumption (<math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>))<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The condition <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> is a regularity assumption on <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> or equivalently, on the training distribution. Such an assumption fails on raw empirical measures which have no Lebesgue densities and hence no classical scores, and may also not be satisfied for idealized distributions supported on low-dimensional sets. Hence, in such cases, annealing the truncation all the way to zero is not justified by Fisher
information control alone.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.2.2 </span>Case 2: Fresh-data proportion <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and target distribution does not have finite Fisher information</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We distinguish between two alternatives in the case where <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> fails.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">1. <span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Strictly positive truncation floor.</span> A first option is to consider truncation schedules <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{0}^{(N)})_{N\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{0}^{(N)})_{N\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> that are decreasing down to a small positive floor <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\infty}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\infty}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for which Fisher scores remain bounded independently of the regularity of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>, by ((ii)-Proposition <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition E.1 (Fisher control for OU smoothing). ‣ Instability of the reverse diffusion around 𝑡↓0 ‣ E.1 Fisher Information Instability and Properties ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A5.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-t_{\infty}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{\infty}}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq\frac{d}{1-e^{-t_{\infty}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">2. <span id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Coupled annealing of fresh-data and truncation.</span>
A way to remove the finite-Fisher-information requirement on
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> while still letting the truncation time vanish is to
anneal the fresh-data proportion together with the truncation schedule. Consider
the generation-dependent recursion</p>
<table id="A5.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{N+1}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\Bigl(\alpha_{N}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha_{N})\hat{p}^{N}\Bigr),\qquad t_{0}^{(N)}\downarrow 0,\qquad\alpha_{N}\downarrow 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{N+1}=\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}^{(N)}}\Bigl(\alpha_{N}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha_{N})\hat{p}^{N}\Bigr),\qquad t_{0}^{(N)}\downarrow 0,\qquad\alpha_{N}\downarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For any generation <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, linearity of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition B.1 (Basic properties of the OU sampling operator). ‣ Sampling operator on probability measures. ‣ B.1 Diffusion, Ornstein–Uhlenbeck Process and Semigroup ‣ Appendix B Extended Background and Preliminary Results ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>) and convexity of Fisher information (Proposition <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition E.1 (Fisher control for OU smoothing). ‣ Instability of the reverse diffusion around 𝑡↓0 ‣ E.1 Fisher Information Instability and Properties ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A5.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\hat{p}^{N+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\hat{p}^{N+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex152.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J\!\left(\alpha_{N}\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha_{N})\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}\hat{p}^{N}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.481em;" width="0.481em"><mi>J</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J\!\left(\alpha_{N}\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}p_{\mathrm{data}}+(1-\alpha_{N})\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}\hat{p}^{N}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\alpha_{N}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}p_{\mathrm{data}})+(1-\alpha_{N})J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}\hat{p}^{N})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\alpha_{N}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}p_{\mathrm{data}})+(1-\alpha_{N})J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}\hat{p}^{N}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">The first term is the only term involving freshly injected, potentially
irregular data. By the universal OU smoothing bound ((ii) in Proposition <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition E.1 (Fisher control for OU smoothing). ‣ Instability of the reverse diffusion around 𝑡↓0 ‣ E.1 Fisher Information Instability and Properties ‣ Appendix E Self-Regularization and Annealed Truncation ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>),</p>
<table id="A5.Ex154" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{N}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq\alpha_{N}\frac{d}{1-e^{-t_{N}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{N}J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}p_{\mathrm{data}})\leq\alpha_{N}\frac{d}{1-e^{-t_{N}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Consequently, the fresh-data contribution remains uniformly bounded provided</p>
<table id="A5.Ex155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{N\geq 0}\frac{\alpha_{N}}{1-e^{-t_{N}}}&lt;\infty," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{N\geq 0}\frac{\alpha_{N}}{1-e^{-t_{N}}}&lt;\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">or equivalently, since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-e^{-t_{N}}\sim t_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-e^{-t_{N}}\sim t_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{N}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{N}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{N}=\mathcal{O}(t_{N})\qquad\text{as }t_{N}\downarrow 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{N}=\mathcal{O}(t_{N})\qquad\text{as }t_{N}\downarrow 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This condition controls the newly injected raw-data component. To obtain a uniform Fisher bound for the whole training distribution, one must additionally control the synthetic term</p>
<table id="A5.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha_{N})J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}\hat{p}^{N})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha_{N})J(\mathcal{U}_{t_{N}}\hat{p}^{N}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">either by an induction argument, by an explicit unrolling of the recursion, or by imposing a stronger global summability condition on the whole sequence of weights and accumulated smoothing times. Thus, coupled annealing of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> provides an alternative to <math id="A5.SS2.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(p_{\mathrm{data}})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for the fresh component, but full uniform Fisher control requires the same convexity argument to be applied to all mixture components.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We validate our theoretical results on (i) synthetic 2D Gaussian mixtures, where the limiting distribution <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> (Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Collapse distribution: existence, uniqueness, and explicit form). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) can be computed in closed form and serves as a controlled environment for Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 3.2 (Limiting behaviors). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>; (ii) CIFAR-10 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite> with fixed truncation, where we test the geometric rate of convergence to <math id="A6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> (Theorems <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Collapse distribution: existence, uniqueness, and explicit form). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Geometric convergence and stability). ‣ Concentration around 𝑝_∞^⋆ ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>) and the spectral structure of collapse (Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Spectral representation of the collapse distribution). ‣ 3.1 Spectral decomposition of the collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>); and (iii) CIFAR-10 with annealed truncation schedules, where we test the recovery of <math id="A6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> predicted by Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Asymptotic effect of generation-dependent truncation). ‣ Generation-dependent truncation ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. All synthetic two-dimensional experiments were run on CPU workers, whereas image experiments (on CIFAR-10) were run on a single NVIDIA RTX 6000 Blackwell GPU with 96GB memory; a full 8-generation CIFAR-10 recursive training run required approximately 12 hours of wall-clock time.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Synthetic 2D Gaussian mixtures</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We set <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> to a three-component isotropic mixture in <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and run the error-free recursion (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) for <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> generations at <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\{0.1,0.5,0.9\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\{0.1,0.5,0.9\}</annotation></semantics></math>, using a Variance Preserving SDE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite> with <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math> so that the OU semigroup matches our analysis exactly and the contraction constant <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa=\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}</annotation></semantics></math> holds without approximation. For <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> a Gaussian mixture, <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Theorem 3.1 (Collapse distribution: existence, uniqueness, and explicit form). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) is itself a countably-infinite mixture of Gaussians that can be sampled from KL divergences and admit accurate Monte-Carlo estimators.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Limiting behaviors (Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 3.2 (Limiting behaviors). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>).</span> Figure <a href="#A6.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ F.1 Synthetic 2D Gaussian mixtures ‣ Appendix F Experiments ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> sweeps <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[0.02,0.98]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.98</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[0.02,0.98]</annotation></semantics></math> at fixed <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (left and center panels) and <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\in[0,5]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\in[0,5]</annotation></semantics></math> at fixed <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (right panel), computing <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> analytically at each grid point. The three predicted limits are recovered: <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(p_{\infty}^{\star}\,\|\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}})\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(p_{\infty}^{\star}\,\|\,\mathcal{U}_{t_{0}}p_{\mathrm{data}})\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(p_{\infty}^{\star}\,\|\,\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}))\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(p_{\infty}^{\star}\,\|\,\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}))\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(p_{\infty}^{\star}\,\|\,p_{\mathrm{data}})\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(p_{\infty}^{\star}\,\|\,p_{\mathrm{data}})\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, with strict positivity at every interior <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,t_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,t_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Truncation schedules (Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Asymptotic effect of generation-dependent truncation). ‣ Generation-dependent truncation ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>).</span> Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> compares four truncation schedules over <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> generations at <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\{0.1,0.5,0.9\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\{0.1,0.5,0.9\}</annotation></semantics></math>: a fixed schedule <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(i)}\equiv t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(i)}\equiv t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, a shifted schedule with <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(i)}\to t_{\infty}=0.2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(i)}\to t_{\infty}=0.2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and two summable annealed schedules <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(i)}=t_{0}/(1+i)^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(i)}=t_{0}/(1+i)^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The fixed schedule plateaus at the predicted irreducible floor <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the shifted schedule plateaus at the lower predicted limit <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})},p_{\mathrm{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(p_{\infty}^{(t_{\infty})},p_{\mathrm{data}})</annotation></semantics></math>, both consistent with the asymptotic statement of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Asymptotic effect of generation-dependent truncation). ‣ Generation-dependent truncation ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. The two summable annealed schedules drive the recursion back toward <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with the decay rate increasing in <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, confirming that recursive compounding is asymptotically eliminated whenever <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}^{(i)}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}^{(i)}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. The qualitative behavior is consistent across <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, with smaller <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> producing slower convergence, as expected from the contraction constant <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa=\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.13796v1/05_limiting_behaviors.svg" id="A6.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/107;" width="476" height="107"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A6.F4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Limiting behaviours of <math id="A6.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> on a 2D Gaussian mixture.<span id="A6.F4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The closed-form Neumann-series representation of <math id="A6.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> (Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Collapse distribution: existence, uniqueness, and explicit form). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) recovers the three predicted limits of Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 3.2 (Limiting behaviors). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>: convergence to a single OU-smoothed copy of <math id="A6.F4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.F4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> (i), convergence to the standard Gaussian as <math id="A6.F4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> (ii), and recovery of <math id="A6.F4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.F4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> (iii); strict positivity at all interior <math id="A6.F4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,t_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,t_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is visible in panel (iii).</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.13796v1/fig_truncationvf.svg" id="A6.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/131;" width="476" height="131"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F5.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A6.F5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Truncation time controls the severity of collapse (CIFAR-10 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>).<span id="A6.F5.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
<span id="A6.F5.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Left</span>: FID between the limiting collapse distribution <math id="A6.F5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and the data distribution <math id="A6.F5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a function of the reverse-time truncation <math id="A6.F5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, for several fresh-data proportions <math id="A6.F5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. Increasing <math id="A6.F5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> amplifies the bias induced by each recursive generation, and the effect is strongest when <math id="A6.F5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is small, i.e. when synthetic samples dominate the next training distribution.
<span id="A6.F5.7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Right</span>: absolute radial Fourier power of <math id="A6.F5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, divided by that of <math id="A6.F5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for increasing values of <math id="A6.F5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the ratio is not normalized to unit total spectral mass, values above one indicate excess broadband power induced by the truncation noise rather than a redistribution of fixed spectral energy. As <math id="A6.F5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the ratio approaches one, consistently with the recovery of
<math id="A6.F5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>CIFAR-10: limiting collapse and spectral signature</h3>

<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a U-Net <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite> score network
with self-attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite> at the two coarsest spatial
scales, trained with the min-SNR-<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> objective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite> (<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=5</annotation></semantics></math>)
and EMA decay <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9999</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9999</annotation></semantics></math>. Each generation is trained for <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math> epochs at
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{lr}=2\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>lr</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{lr}=2\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> with cosine decay, batch size <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math>, and
AdamW <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> (weight decay <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>). The truncation time is fixed
at <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>. At generation <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the training loader returns each
example with probability <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> from CIFAR-10 and probability <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>
from a pool of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> samples drawn from generation <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-1</annotation></semantics></math> via
DPM-Solver++ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite> with <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> steps. We run <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> generations
for <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\{0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\{0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9\}</annotation></semantics></math> and report metrics averaged
across <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> seeds. FID <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> is computed against the full
CIFAR-10 training split using <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>30,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> generated samples per checkpoint.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Empirical proxy for <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The collapse distribution <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is not directly accessible, since <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> is unknown. We consider an empirical proxy of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> by approximating <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}\approx\hat{p}_{\mathrm{trained}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>trained</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}\approx\hat{p}_{\mathrm{trained}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{\mathrm{trained}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>trained</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{\mathrm{trained}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a well-trained diffusion model on CIFAR-10, solely on real data, and from which one can thus sample. This allows to sample from <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> by leveraging its closed-form formula (infinite mixture of Gaussian-smoothed version of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>), which is required to compute the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FID}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>FID</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FID}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">High-frequency energy.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a probability measure <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> on
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{3\times 32\times 32}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{3\times 32\times 32}</annotation></semantics></math> approximated by <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{spec}}=2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>spec</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{spec}}=2000</annotation></semantics></math>
samples <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{N_{\mathrm{spec}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>spec</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{N_{\mathrm{spec}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the
<em id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">high-frequency energy</em> as</p>
<table id="A6.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{HF}(p)\;:=\;\frac{1}{N_{\mathrm{spec}}}\sum_{j=1}^{N_{\mathrm{spec}}}\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\sum_{\mathbf{k}\in\mathcal{A}}\bigl|\mathcal{F}[\bar{x}^{(j)}](\mathbf{k})\bigr|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>HF</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>spec</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>spec</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{HF}(p)\;:=\;\frac{1}{N_{\mathrm{spec}}}\sum_{j=1}^{N_{\mathrm{spec}}}\frac{1}{|\mathcal{A}|}\sum_{\mathbf{k}\in\mathcal{A}}\bigl|\mathcal{F}[\bar{x}^{(j)}](\mathbf{k})\bigr|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{x}^{(j)}=0.2989\,x^{(j)}_{R}+0.5870\,x^{(j)}_{G}+0.1140\,x^{(j)}_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.2989</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.5870</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.1140</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}^{(j)}=0.2989\,x^{(j)}_{R}+0.5870\,x^{(j)}_{G}+0.1140\,x^{(j)}_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>
is the luminance projection of the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample, <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is the
zero-centered 2D discrete Fourier transform, and <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}:=\{\mathbf{k}\in\mathbb{Z}^{2}:\|\mathbf{k}\|_{2}\geq 15\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}:=\{\mathbf{k}\in\mathbb{Z}^{2}:\|\mathbf{k}\|_{2}\geq 15\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the
high-frequency annulus in the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math> Fourier plane (cutoff radius
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\star}=15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\star}=15</annotation></semantics></math>, slightly below the Nyquist limit of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>). We define the
<em id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">high-frequency deficit</em> of generation <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A6.E71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{D}_{\mathrm{HF}}(\hat{p}^{N})\;:=\;1-\frac{\mathrm{HF}(\hat{p}^{N})}{\mathrm{HF}(p_{\mathrm{data}})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>HF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>HF</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>HF</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{D}_{\mathrm{HF}}(\hat{p}^{N})\;:=\;1-\frac{\mathrm{HF}(\hat{p}^{N})}{\mathrm{HF}(p_{\mathrm{data}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{HF}(p_{\mathrm{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>HF</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{HF}(p_{\mathrm{data}})</annotation></semantics></math> is computed on <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{spec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>spec</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{spec}}</annotation></semantics></math>
real CIFAR-10 images. Larger <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{D}_{\mathrm{HF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>HF</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{D}_{\mathrm{HF}}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates stronger
loss of fine-scale Fourier content relative to the data, providing a real-image
proxy for the high-degree Hermite-mode attenuation predicted by
Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Spectral representation of the collapse distribution). ‣ 3.1 Spectral decomposition of the collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Convergence to <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>
(Figure <a href="#S4.F3.sf1" title="Figure 3(a) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ Self-regularization regime ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a>, Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Geometric convergence and stability). ‣ Concentration around 𝑝_∞^⋆ ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>).</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FID}(\hat{p}^{N},\hat{p}_{\infty}^{\,(\alpha)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>FID</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FID}(\hat{p}^{N},\hat{p}_{\infty}^{\,(\alpha)})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{\infty}^{\,(\alpha)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{\infty}^{\,(\alpha)}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the limiting distribution of the recursion with proportion <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, across the first <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> recursive generations for each <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. The contraction is fastest at large <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and slowest at <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, where the trajectory is clearly transient: the iterate drops from <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FID}\approx 33" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>FID</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>33</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FID}\approx 33</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FID}\approx 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>FID</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FID}\approx 5</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=8</annotation></semantics></math>. By the eighth generation, all
trajectories settle near a common empirical floor of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FID}\approx 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>FID</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FID}\approx 5</annotation></semantics></math>, which we interpret as the residual <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FID}(\hat{p}_{\infty}^{\,(\alpha)},\,p_{\infty}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>FID</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FID}(\hat{p}_{\infty}^{\,(\alpha)},\,p_{\infty}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> plus measurement noise from finite-sample FID. This pattern is consistent with the contraction-rate ordering predicted by <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa(\alpha)=\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(\alpha)=\sqrt{1-\alpha}\,e^{-t_{0}/2}</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Geometric convergence and stability). ‣ Concentration around 𝑝_∞^⋆ ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> and with the stability statement (ii) of the same theorem.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Spectral signature
(Figure <a href="#S4.F3.sf2" title="Figure 3(b) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ Self-regularization regime ‣ 4 Mitigating Model Collapse with Annealed Truncation Schedules ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a>,
Propositions <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Spectral representation of the collapse distribution). ‣ 3.1 Spectral decomposition of the collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 5.3 (Mode-dependent error propagation). ‣ Spectral Decomposition in the Learned Regime ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>).</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The high-frequency deficit <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{D}_{\mathrm{HF}}(\hat{p}^{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>HF</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{D}_{\mathrm{HF}}(\hat{p}^{N})</annotation></semantics></math> across the first <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> generations is monotone increasing in both <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. At <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, the deficit reaches <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 0.5</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that roughly half of the high-frequency Fourier energy of CIFAR-10 has been suppressed; at <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, the deficit remains below <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.15</annotation></semantics></math> over the same horizon. The mode-dependent contraction rate <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{\mathbf{n}}(\alpha)=(1-\alpha)\,e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{\mathbf{n}}(\alpha)=(1-\alpha)\,e^{-|\mathbf{n}|t_{0}/2}</annotation></semantics></math> in Proposition <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 5.3 (Mode-dependent error propagation). ‣ Spectral Decomposition in the Learned Regime ‣ 5 Robustness of Limiting Distribution in the Presence of Errors ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> predicts exactly this joint monotonicity in <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> (faster compounding for larger <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbf{n}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{n}|</annotation></semantics></math>) and in <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (smaller fresh-data injection magnifies attenuation).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Truncation severity
(Figure <a href="#A6.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ F.1 Synthetic 2D Gaussian mixtures ‣ Appendix F Experiments ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary 3.2 (Limiting behaviors). ‣ Collapse distribution ‣ 3 Limiting Collapse Distribution in the Error-free Regime ‣ Recursively Trained Diffusion Models: Limiting Collapse Distribution and Spectral Characterization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>).</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The FID gap <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FID}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>FID</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FID}(p_{\infty}^{\star},p_{\mathrm{data}})</annotation></semantics></math> grows with <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and decays toward zero as <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, while the radial Fourier spectrum of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> approaches that of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> at all frequencies as <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> shrinks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
